IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc11-definitions`

-- ccc11-general.l4 -- Part VIII.1, sections 320.36 to 320.4 (General Provisions: use of samples and results, refusal to take a sample, regulations, approvals, designations) of the Criminal Code (Canada),
-- R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46. LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30);
-- it is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- A prohibition or a duty answers JUST TRUE when it applies on the stated facts and JUST FALSE where its own "if", "except" or "unless" is unmet or met (marginal readings (a) in NOTES.md, with the other reading);
-- a power ("may") answers JUST TRUE when its gates hold and NOTHING when one does not (ruling of 2026-11-12). Section 320.38 (regulations) is machinery (inert, reason 2): its six paragraphs name the numbers
-- and tests that other sections take as inputs, and they are quoted at the end of this file.

-- Line 6476: the division heading "General Provisions": inert (reason 1, a heading).
-- src:6476 | General Provisions
§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.36: use of bodily substances and of results`

-- The party of a prohibition that binds "no person": the core's `Party` has no constructor for an unnamed person, so this part declares one under its own prefix (NEEDS-CORE.md asks the lead to hoist it).
DECLARE `s 320.36 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.36 any person`

DECLARE `s 320.36 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 320.36(1) use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part`
    `s 320.36(2) use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance`

-- (1): "No person shall use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for any purpose other than for an analysis under this Part."
-- src:6477 | Unauthorized use of bodily substance
-- src:6478 | 320.36 (1) No person shall use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for any purpose other than for an analysis under this Part.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(1) (src:6477-6478)
GIVEN `the bodily substance was obtained under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is for a purpose other than for an analysis under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.36(1) the use of the bodily substance is prohibited` MEANS
    IF `the bodily substance was obtained under this Part` AND `the use is for a purpose other than for an analysis under this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for any purpose other than for an analysis under this Part" (the prohibition's own conditions unmet)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(1) (src:6477-6478)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 320.36 party` `s 320.36 action`
`s 320.36(1) no person shall use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for another purpose` MEANS
    PARTY `s 320.36 any person`
    SHANT `s 320.36(1) use a bodily substance obtained under this Part for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 320.36 any person` BECAUSE "a person used a bodily substance obtained under this Part for a purpose other than an analysis under this Part"

-- (3): "The results of an evaluation, test or analysis referred to in subsection (2) may be disclosed to the person to whom they relate, and may be disclosed to any other person if the results are made anonymous and
-- the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes." A permission: NOTHING when no gate holds.
-- src:6481 | Exception
-- src:6482 | (3) The results of an evaluation, test or analysis referred to in subsection (2) may be disclosed to the person to whom they relate, and may be disclosed to any other person if the results are made anonymous and the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(3) (src:6481-6482)
GIVEN `the results are of an evaluation, test or analysis referred to in subsection 320.36(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to the person to whom they relate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the results are made anonymous` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.36(3) the results may be disclosed` MEANS
    IF `the results are of an evaluation, test or analysis referred to in subsection 320.36(2)` AND (`the disclosure is to the person to whom they relate` OR (`the results are made anonymous` AND `the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be disclosed to the person to whom they relate, and may be disclosed to any other person if the results are made anonymous and the disclosure is made for statistical or research purposes"

-- (2): "No person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of any evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance, except for the purpose of the
-- administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs and/or alcohol and/or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment." Subject to the exception of subsection (3).
-- src:6479 | Unauthorized use or disclosure of results
-- src:6480 | (2) No person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of any evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance, except for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs and/or alcohol and/or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(2) (src:6479-6480)
GIVEN `the results were obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs and/or alcohol and/or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is permitted by subsection 320.36(3), by s 320.36(3)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.36(2) the use or disclosure of the results is prohibited` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the results were obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance` AND `the person uses, discloses or allows the disclosure of the results`))
       OR `it is for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act related to drugs and/or alcohol and/or to the operation of a motor vehicle, vessel, aircraft or railway equipment`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of any evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance, except for the purpose of the administration or enforcement of a federal or provincial Act" (the prohibition's own conditions unmet, or the exception met)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the disclosure is permitted by subsection 320.36(3), by s 320.36(3)`
         WHEN JUST permitted THEN (IF permitted THEN JUST FALSE ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be disclosed to the person to whom they relate" (subsection (3) permits the disclosure: the exception)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE   -- subsection (3) is a grant that answers NOTHING when its gate is unmet, so on these facts no exception is made out and the prohibition of (2) stands (fork F26 in NOTES.md)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(2) (src:6479-6480)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 320.36 party` `s 320.36 action`
`s 320.36(2) no person shall use or disclose the results for another purpose` MEANS
    PARTY `s 320.36 any person`
    SHANT `s 320.36(2) use, disclose or allow the disclosure of the results obtained under this Part of an evaluation, physical coordination test or analysis of a bodily substance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 320.36 any person` BECAUSE "a person used or disclosed the results obtained under this Part otherwise than as subsection 320.36(2) allows"

-- (4): "Everyone who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) commits an offence punishable on summary conviction." The punishment is not stated: the general penalty of section 787(1) is an input (PLAN.md section 6, seam).
-- src:6483 | Offence
-- src:6484 | (4) Everyone who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) commits an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(4) (src:6483-6484)
GIVEN `the person contravenes subsection 320.36(1), by s 320.36(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person contravenes subsection 320.36(2), by s 320.36(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.36(4) everyone commits an offence who contravenes subsection 320.36(1) or (2)` MEANS
    `s 320.11 helper: either holds` `the person contravenes subsection 320.36(1), by s 320.36(1)` `the person contravenes subsection 320.36(2), by s 320.36(2)`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Everyone who contravenes subsection (1) or (2) commits an offence" (neither is contravened)
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(4) (src:6483-6484)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 320.36(4) the punishment for an offence under subsection 320.36(4)` MEANS
    `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 320.36(4) (src:6483-6484)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 320.36(4) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.37: refusal to take a sample; no liability`

-- (1): "No qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood from a person for the purposes of this Part if they have
-- a reasonable excuse for refusing to do so." The immunity applies where the "if" holds; JUST FALSE where it does not.
-- src:6485 | Refusal to take sample
-- src:6486 | 320.37 (1) No qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood from a person for the purposes of this Part if they have a reasonable excuse for refusing to do so.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.37(1) (src:6485-6486)
GIVEN `the person is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the only ground of the charge is their refusal to take a sample of blood from a person for the purposes of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a reasonable excuse for refusing to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.37(1) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall not be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the only ground of the charge is their refusal to take a sample of blood from a person for the purposes of this Part` AND `they have a reasonable excuse for refusing to do so`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician shall be found guilty of an offence by reason only of their refusal to take a sample of blood from a person for the purposes of this Part if they have a reasonable excuse for refusing to do so" (the "if" unmet: this subsection gives no immunity on these facts)
    ELSE `s 320.11 helper: either holds` `the person is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples`
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): an input that the answering section leaves not covered gives NOTHING (carried through the Kleene helper)

-- (2): "No qualified medical practitioner, and no qualified technician, who takes a sample of blood from a person under this Part incurs any liability for doing anything necessary to take the sample that was done with
-- reasonable care and skill." Asks whether they incur liability: JUST FALSE where the stated facts hold; the immunity does not reach anything else (NOTHING).
-- src:6487 | No liability
-- src:6488 | (2) No qualified medical practitioner, and no qualified technician, who takes a sample of blood from a person under this Part incurs any liability for doing anything necessary to take the sample that was done with reasonable care and skill.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.37(2) (src:6487-6488)
GIVEN `the person is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `they take a sample of blood from a person under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what was done was necessary to take the sample` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was done with reasonable care and skill` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.37(2) the qualified medical practitioner or qualified technician incurs liability for doing what was necessary to take the sample` MEANS
    IF `they take a sample of blood from a person under this Part` AND `what was done was necessary to take the sample` AND `it was done with reasonable care and skill`
       AND `s 320.11 helper: either holds` `the person is a qualified medical practitioner, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified medical practitioner` `the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples, by s 320.11 the person is a qualified technician in respect of blood samples` EQUALS (JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No qualified medical practitioner, and no qualified technician, who takes a sample of blood from a person under this Part incurs any liability for doing anything necessary to take the sample that was done with reasonable care and skill"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for doing anything necessary to take the sample that was done with reasonable care and skill"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.38: regulations (machinery)`

-- Section 320.38 ("The Governor in Council may make regulations (a) prescribing the qualifications required for a peace officer to act as an evaluating officer and respecting the training of evaluating officers;
-- (b) prescribing the blood drug concentration for a drug for the purpose of paragraph 320.14(1)(c); (c) ... (d) ... (e) prescribing the physical coordination tests ...; (f) prescribing the tests to be conducted and
-- procedures to be followed during an evaluation") is a regulation-making power: machinery, inert (reason 2). Its effects are inputs elsewhere: the qualifications (s 320.11 "evaluating officer"), the concentrations
-- (s 320.14(1)(c), (d), (4)), the tests (s 320.27(1)(a)) and the evaluation procedure (s 320.28(2)(a)).
-- src:6489 | Regulations
-- src:6490 | 320.38 The Governor in Council may make regulations
-- src:6491 | (a) prescribing the qualifications required for a peace officer to act as an evaluating officer and respecting the training of evaluating officers;
-- src:6492 | (b) prescribing the blood drug concentration for a drug for the purpose of paragraph 320.14(1)(c);
-- src:6493 | (c) prescribing a blood alcohol concentration and a blood drug concentration for a drug for the purposes of paragraph 320.14(1)(d);
-- src:6494 | (d) prescribing the blood drug concentration for a drug for the purpose of subsection 320.14(4);
-- src:6495 | (e) prescribing the physical coordination tests to be conducted under paragraph 320.27(1)(a); and
-- src:6496 | (f) prescribing the tests to be conducted and procedures to be followed during an evaluation under paragraph 320.28(2)(a) and the forms to be used in recording the results of the evaluation.

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.39: approval by the Attorney General of Canada`

-- "The Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve (a) a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person's blood; (b) equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person's body;
-- (c) an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person's breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration; and (d) a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person's blood for analysis."
-- Four powers: each answers JUST TRUE where the thing is of the kind the paragraph names and NOTHING otherwise. The effect of an approval is in s 320.11 (the four "approved" definitions).
-- src:6497 | Approval — Attorney General of Canada
-- src:6498 | 320.39 The Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve
-- src:6499 | (a) a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood;
-- src:6500 | (b) equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body;
-- src:6501 | (c) an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration; and
-- src:6502 | (d) a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.39 (src:6497-6502)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.39(a) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the device` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` AND `it is a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve (a) a device that is designed to ascertain the presence of alcohol in a person’s blood"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.39(b) (src:6497-6500)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.39(b) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the equipment` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` AND `it is equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) equipment that is designed to ascertain the presence of a drug in a person’s body"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.39(c) (src:6497-6498)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.39(c) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the instrument` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` AND `it is an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) an instrument that is designed to receive and make an analysis of a sample of a person’s breath to determine their blood alcohol concentration"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.39(d) (src:6497-6498)
GIVEN `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.39(d) the Attorney General of Canada may, by order, approve the container` MEANS
    IF `the Attorney General of Canada acts by order` AND `it is a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) a container that is designed to receive a sample of a person’s blood for analysis"

§ `Part VIII.1 -- section 320.4: designation by the Attorney General`

-- "The Attorney General may designate (a) a person as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to operate an approved instrument; (b) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, (i) to take samples
-- of blood, or (ii) to analyze samples of bodily substances; and (c) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument."
-- Four powers. Paragraph (a) names "a person" only (no class); (b) and (c) name "a person or class of persons". NOTHING where a gate is unmet.
-- src:6503 | Designation — Attorney General
-- src:6504 | 320.4 The Attorney General may designate
-- src:6505 | (a) a person as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to operate an approved instrument;
-- src:6506 | (b) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part,
-- src:6507 | (i) to take samples of blood, or
-- src:6508 | (ii) to analyze samples of bodily substances; and
-- src:6509 | (c) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument.
@ref Criminal Code s 320.4 (src:6503-6509)
GIVEN `the designation is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to operate an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.4(a) the Attorney General may designate the person as qualified to operate an approved instrument` MEANS
    IF `the designation is made by the Attorney General` AND `the designation is of a person` AND `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to operate an approved instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General may designate (a) a person as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to operate an approved instrument"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.4(b)(i) (src:6503-6507)
GIVEN `the designation is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is of a person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to take samples of blood` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.4(b)(i) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to take samples of blood` MEANS
    IF `the designation is made by the Attorney General` AND `the designation is of a person or class of persons` AND `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to take samples of blood`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, (i) to take samples of blood"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.4(b)(ii) (src:6503-6508)
GIVEN `the designation is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is of a person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to analyze samples of bodily substances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.4(b)(ii) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to analyze samples of bodily substances` MEANS
    IF `the designation is made by the Attorney General` AND `the designation is of a person or class of persons` AND `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to analyze samples of bodily substances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(ii) to analyze samples of bodily substances"

@ref Criminal Code s 320.4(c) (src:6503-6509)
GIVEN `the designation is made by the Attorney General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is of a person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 320.4(c) the Attorney General may designate the person or class of persons as qualified to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument` MEANS
    IF `the designation is made by the Attorney General` AND `the designation is of a person or class of persons` AND `the designation is as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) a person or class of persons as qualified, for the purposes of this Part, to certify that an alcohol standard is suitable for use with an approved instrument"
